.TH PUCI 1 "November 2026" "puci 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
puci \- minimal AI coding agent for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B puci
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B puci
.RI [ options ]
.B run
.I prompt
.br
.B puci doctor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B puci
talks to a language model and lets it read, write and edit files and run
commands in a
.IR workspace ,
asking before anything that changes your system.
On a terminal it starts a full\-screen interface (TUI); otherwise, or with
.BR \-\-no\-tui ,
a line\-mode REPL.
.B run
performs one non\-interactive turn and streams the answer to standard output.
.B doctor
checks the configuration, the key and a live round trip to the provider.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-cwd " " \fIdir\fR
Use
.I dir
as the workspace (default: the current directory).
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Approve every tool call without asking. Writes outside the workspace are
still refused. Use only in sandboxes and CI.
.TP
.BR \-\-plan ", " \-\-dry\-run
Plan mode: file changes are simulated, nothing is written.
.TP
.BI \-\-session " id"
Use or create the named session.
.TP
.BR \-\-resume " [" latest | \fIid\fR ]
Continue a saved session.
.TP
.B \-\-trust\-project\-mcp
Start the MCP servers declared in this project's
.IR .puci.toml .
Without it they are listed but not started, because starting one runs a
command from the repository.
.TP
.BR \-\-tui ", " \-\-no\-tui
Force the full\-screen interface, or the line\-mode REPL.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-sessions
List saved sessions.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.SH WORKSPACE AND APPROVAL
Reading inside the workspace needs no approval; reading outside it always
asks. Writing or editing files outside the workspace, and running a command
with its working directory outside it, are refused. Symbolic links and
.B ..
are resolved first. Every shell command asks for approval, because the
command itself can reach any file. Starting puci in your home directory or
.B /
prints a warning.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPENROUTER_API_KEY
OpenRouter key; also sets the base URL to OpenRouter.
.TP
.BR PUCI_API_KEY ", " PUCI_BASE_URL ", " PUCI_MODEL
Provider key, endpoint (any OpenAI\-compatible URL such as Ollama or
llama.cpp, or Anthropic) and model.
.TP
.B PUCI_AUTO_APPROVE=1
Same as
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B PUCI_THEME=light|dark
Override the detected terminal background.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/puci/config.toml
User configuration: base_url, model, api_key, MCP servers.
.TP
.I .puci.toml
Project configuration. Keys and credentials are refused here.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/puci/sessions/
Saved conversations (mode 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/puci/history
Prompt history (mode 0600).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on a runtime or provider error, 2 on a usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
export OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk\-or\-...
puci doctor
cd ~/src/project && puci
puci \-C ~/src/project run "add a \-\-verbose flag"
PUCI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1 PUCI_MODEL=qwen3 puci
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libpuci (3)
.PP
https://github.com/uzunenes/puci
